problem:
Problem description
- There is a single transportation planning horizon $$\mathcal{T}$$ and a set of delivery locations $$\mathcal{S}=\{1,\ldots,S\}$$ served from a warehouse.
- Transportation is available through a set of modes $$\mathcal{M}$$, with each mode indexed by $$m$$. In the generic model, each mode has a per-trip capacity, a per-trip pollution contribution, and may have additional usage restrictions.
- Demand may be provided either as an aggregate requirement $$D$$ or as location-level demands $$d_s$$ for each $$s \in \mathcal{S}$$.
- Each mode $$m \in \mathcal{M}$$ has a trip capacity $$c_m$$ and a pollution cost per trip $$p_m$$.
- The planning goal is to satisfy transportation demand while minimizing the total pollution generated by all trips.
- The planner must ensure that the total delivered quantity is sufficient to cover demand.
- The planner must ensure that the total pollution does not exceed the allowable pollution budget $$P^{\max}$$.
- The planner must ensure that the truck mode is used at least a minimum number of times, denoted by $$L_{\text{truck}}$$.
- The planner must respect the mutual exclusivity rule that the van mode and the electric vehicle mode cannot both be used in the same plan.
- Each mode’s transported quantity must be consistent with the number of trips assigned to that mode and its trip capacity.
- All trip counts must be nonnegative integers, and any mode-activation indicators must be binary.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_m$$: the integer number of trips assigned to transportation mode $$m \in \mathcal{M}$$.
  - $$z_m$$: a binary indicator equal to $$1$$ if mode $$m$$ is used and $$0$$ otherwise.
  - $$q_m$$: the quantity transported using mode $$m \in \mathcal{M}$$.
  - $$Q$$: the total quantity delivered across all modes.
  - $$P$$: the total pollution generated by the transportation plan.

Input Format
{
  "planning_horizon": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{T}$$",
    "description": "Set of planning periods."
  },
  "sales_points": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{S}$$",
    "description": "Set of delivery locations indexed by $$s$$.",
    "shape": "$$S$$"
  },
  "modes": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{M}$$",
    "description": "Set of transportation modes indexed by $$m$$.",
    "elements": ["truck", "van", "motorcycle", "electric_vehicle"]
  },
  "aggregate_demand": {
    "symbol": "$$D$$",
    "description": "Total quantity that must be delivered across the planning horizon."
  },
  "demand_by_sales_point": {
    "symbol": "$$d_s$$",
    "description": "Optional location-level demand for each $$s \\in \\mathcal{S}$$.",
    "shape": "$$S$$",
    "optional": true
  },
  "trip_capacity": {
    "symbol": "$$c_m$$",
    "description": "Maximum quantity that can be transported in one trip of mode $$m$$.",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{M}|$$"
  },
  "pollution_per_trip": {
    "symbol": "$$p_m$$",
    "description": "Pollution generated by one trip of mode $$m$$.",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{M}|$$"
  },
  "max_total_pollution": {
    "symbol": "$$P^{\\max}$$",
    "description": "Upper bound on total pollution."
  },
  "minimum_truck_trips": {
    "symbol": "$$L_{\\text{truck}}$$",
    "description": "Minimum required number of truck trips."
  },
  "exclusive_mode_pairs": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{E}$$",
    "description": "Set of mode pairs that cannot be used together in the same plan.",
    "format": "List of ordered or unordered pairs of mode names"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "status": {
    "symbol": "$$\\text{status}$$",
    "description": "Solution status such as $$\\text{optimal}$$, $$\\text{feasible}$$, or $$\\text{infeasible}$$."
  },
  "trips_by_mode": {
    "symbol": "$$x_m$$",
    "description": "Integer number of trips assigned to each mode $$m \\in \\mathcal{M}$$.",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{M}|$$"
  },
  "mode_usage": {
    "symbol": "$$z_m$$",
    "description": "Binary indicator showing whether each mode $$m \\in \\mathcal{M}$$ is used.",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{M}|$$"
  },
  "quantity_by_mode": {
    "symbol": "$$q_m$$",
    "description": "Quantity transported by each mode $$m \\in \\mathcal{M}$$.",
    "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{M}|$$"
  },
  "total_delivered": {
    "symbol": "$$Q$$",
    "description": "Total quantity delivered across all modes."
  },
  "total_pollution": {
    "symbol": "$$P$$",
    "description": "Total pollution generated by the transportation plan."
  },
  "objective_value": {
    "symbol": "$$P^*$$",
    "description": "Minimum achievable total pollution."
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "planning_horizon": {
    "symbol": "T",
    "description": "Single planning period."
  },
  "sales_points": 3,
  "aggregate_demand": 1800,
  "modes": {
    "truck": {
      "capacity_per_trip": 100,
      "pollution_per_trip": 100,
      "minimum_trips": 10
    },
    "van": {
      "capacity_per_trip": 80,
      "pollution_per_trip": 50
    },
    "motorcycle": {
      "capacity_per_trip": 40,
      "pollution_per_trip": 10
    },
    "electric_vehicle": {
      "capacity_per_trip": 60,
      "pollution_per_trip": 0
    }
  },
  "exclusive_mode_pairs": [
    ["van", "electric_vehicle"]
  ],
  "max_total_pollution": 2000
}
